      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "If $A$ is false and $B$ is false, then $A⇔B$ is\n\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "According to the definition of the biconditional, \n\n- $A⇔B$ is true if $A⇒B$ **and** $B⇒A.$ Otherwise, it is false.\n\n- In other words, $A⇔B$ is true if $A$ and $B$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nSo, when $A=\\text{F}$ and $B=\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A⇔B) & =(\\text{F}⇔\\text{F}) \\\\  & =\\text{T}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe complete truth table is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A⇔B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n|  |  |  |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |",
